1
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:26,860
Aiming for Kasuga, floating on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:34,000
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too.

3
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:42,220
Onto the head of the
carpenter I was choking,

4
00:00:42,220 --> 00:00:48,440
they laughed that I was still a brat.

5
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:55,560
Wherever spirit stirs,
there's Katsushika Kameari.

6
00:00:55,560 --> 00:01:02,540
Even with a yawn,
the unchanging streets feel strangely kind.

7
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:14,640
From a pointed hat's water bottle,
on to the shop of interpretations.

8
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,780
The sun sets.

9
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:25,240
Tomorrow will end this way too, won't it.

10
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:30,320
Katsushika, Shibamata,
losing even happiness again.

11
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:33,840
Because I'm a fool who finally realized it.

12
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:41,700
Fierce battle! A great war of relations!

13
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,540
How many 8mm tapes do we have?

14
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:47,600
Twelve.

15
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:50,020
And the SmartMedia cards?

16
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:52,460
Ten 16-meg ones.

17
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:53,700
That should be enough.

18
00:01:53,700 --> 00:01:57,120
And don't forget a dozen
6-volt lithium batteries.

19
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,020
Got it.

20
00:01:58,940 --> 00:01:59,760
Good morning.

21
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:02,300
Hey, senpai, what are you doing?

22
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:04,740
On the station's staff trip next time,
we're going to the sea, right?

23
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:07,580
That's when we'll use this to snap
up beautiful women in swimsuits.

24
00:02:07,580 --> 00:02:10,520
After all, it's our once-a-year eye candy.

25
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:12,060
I'm looking forward to it.

26
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:15,140
But this year's staff
trip is to the mountains.

27
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:19,940
What? That's ridiculous!

28
00:02:19,940 --> 00:02:23,380
I'm pretty sure the station's
bulletin board said that.

29
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:26,860
The staff trip has always been decided as the beach,
hasn't it?

30
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:30,320
You won't find any bikini
beauties if we go to the mountains!

31
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:33,640
When a big wave hits a beauty,
her bikini slips

32
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:36,040
and we won't even get to
see a wardrobe malfunction!

33
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:38,500
Don't tell me that. I didn't decide it.

34
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:42,120
Are you really going to take away
the fun of all the male staff?

35
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:46,280
That's exactly why we chose the mountains this time,
because of people like that.

36
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:49,600
So it was you lot behind this after all?

37
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:50,580
Komachi, Naoko

38
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:53,260
I can't accept this.

39
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:55,600
I want to hear the reason for the change.

40
00:02:56,060 --> 00:02:57,220
Not for the likes of you.

41
00:02:57,220 --> 00:03:01,060
We have no intention of showing
you our swimsuit figures, no way!

42
00:03:01,060 --> 00:03:04,020
Yeah, exactly,
being stared at with those lecherous eyes.

43
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:07,680
Who'd want to look at your scrawny bodies?

44
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:11,120
We'll be looking at the
other women in swimsuits.

45
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:13,320
Did you just call our bodies scrawny?

46
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:16,580
Don't talk nonsense when
you've never even seen them!

47
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:20,300
Then show us at the beach.

48
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,660
Fine, we'll show you then!

49
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:24,100
Hey, Komachi.

50
00:03:24,540 --> 00:03:25,340
What?

51
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:27,320
No, we can't.

52
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:30,180
That was close,
I almost fell for his sweet talk.

53
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:32,480
We were so close.

54
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:34,580
No matter what you say,

55
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:37,340
this year's staff trip is decided.
It's the mountains.

56
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:38,740
No way.

57
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:41,900
That's tyranny!
You should hear our opinions too.

58
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:45,140
There's no need to hear them.
It's already been decided.

59
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:46,940
Are you sure you can say that?

60
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:48,120
W-what?

61
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:52,380
You always go on about democracy,
democracy, whenever it suits you.

62
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:56,100
Where's the democracy in this decision?

63
00:03:56,100 --> 00:04:02,120
Besides, democracy is supposed to
respect minority opinions too, isn't it?

64
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:05,920
What kind of democracy
ignores us men's opinions?

65
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:08,740
F-fine, I get it.

66
00:04:08,740 --> 00:04:12,260
Then let's take a fresh
survey of all the staff.

67
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:12,840
Wait!

68
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:16,780
You lot are too good at
rounding up a majority.

69
00:04:16,780 --> 00:04:18,960
It's obvious the beach group will lose.

70
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:20,740
Then what are we supposed to do?

71
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:22,740
Let's settle this fairly with a contest.

72
00:04:22,740 --> 00:04:25,760
Let's decide once and for all whether
we're going to the beach or the mountains.

73
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,180
Fine.

74
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:30,200
Let's settle it with a contest.

75
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:32,720
Fine by me.

76
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:39,620
Ryotsu, how did the discussion go?

77
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:43,300
We're going to settle it with a
contest between us and the Komachi group.

78
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:46,760
We couldn't agree on the contest method,
so we've stalled.

79
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:49,980
But Kankichi Ryotsu is terrible!

80
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:54,540
He keeps suggesting things like
judo and baseball that favor him!

81
00:04:55,700 --> 00:04:58,400
You suggested string
figures and Hyakunin Isshu!

82
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:01,280
Those are all things we're bad at!

83
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:06,140
A fair contest is going to be difficult.

84
00:05:09,020 --> 00:05:12,580
Bakaman! You think we can decide
this important matter that way?

85
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:18,140
That's dangerous!

86
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:21,440
You didn't have to kick!
This isn't kick the can!

87
00:05:22,740 --> 00:05:26,460
Kan-keri... how nostalgic...

88
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:30,080
Didn't we play it with friends
every day when we were kids?

89
00:05:31,260 --> 00:05:33,393
I never lost to anyone at kan-keri,

90
00:05:33,443 --> 00:05:35,900
didn't they call me Kan-keri Komachi?

91
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:39,220
That's it! How about we settle
this with a kan-keri match?

92
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:41,440
You've played it as a kid, right?

93
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:44,600
Foolish Kankichi Ryotsu!

94
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:48,040
Not even knowing I was once
called Kan-keri Komachi!

95
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:51,040
Fine! I accept that challenge!

96
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,520
Foolish Komachi!

97
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:54,838
When I was a kid,

98
00:05:54,888 --> 00:05:58,560
I was even called Ryotsu Kan-keri,
a kan-keri genius!

99
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:02,080
Alright!
Then it's decided, a kan-keri match!

100
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:07,420
Komachi, are you sure about this?

101
00:06:07,420 --> 00:06:08,260
About what?

102
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:09,960
What exactly is kan-keri anyway?

103
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:11,340
You don't know?

104
00:06:11,340 --> 00:06:13,540
Yeah, I don't know either.

105
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:17,160
I lived in America during elementary school, so
I never played it.

106
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:20,100
It's a game for the old neighborhoods
or the countryside, right?

107
00:06:20,100 --> 00:06:21,780
I've never played it either.

108
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:24,920
I used to play it,
but it turns out it's pretty obscure.

109
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:29,180
In other words, isn't it a primitive
game that cavemen would play?

110
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:30,960
So that's how it is.

111
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,980
When I was a kid, everyone played it.

112
00:06:33,980 --> 00:06:36,680
Komachi, you've played it before, right?

113
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:39,840
Actually, I don't know it either.

114
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:42,120
So what do we do, then?

115
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:44,320
There's nothing to be done either way.

116
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:46,140
You already agreed to it once, remember.

117
00:06:46,140 --> 00:06:48,480
Don't go trying to change it now.

118
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:50,400
I know, I know.

119
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:51,300
Komachi.

120
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:55,000
At least teach us the rules, senpai!

121
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,480
We can't have a proper match like this.

122
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,060
Fair point.

123
00:06:59,060 --> 00:06:59,560
Right.

124
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:03,492
Right, then tomorrow we'll gather all
the participants and go over the rules.

125
00:07:03,542 --> 00:07:06,300
Until then, get everyone together.

126
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:07,480
Got it.

127
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:13,220
Sorry to keep you waiting.

128
00:07:13,980 --> 00:07:17,680
I see you didn't run away.
Look, this is our lineup.

129
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:20,323
Terai and Honda are experienced.

130
00:07:20,373 --> 00:07:23,847
Sanedera and Nakagawa have
outstanding athletic ability.

131
00:07:23,897 --> 00:07:25,660
There's no way we can lose.

132
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:29,280
We've put together a powerful team too.

133
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:31,380
Maria

134
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:33,360
Maria-chan is experienced too.

135
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:36,880
I played it back in elementary school,
when I was a boy.

136
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:39,080
Maria, are you planning to betray me?

137
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:41,280
I'm sorry, Ryo-sama.

138
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:44,120
I really want to be of help to you,
Ryo-sama.

139
00:07:44,940 --> 00:07:46,000
But the sea...

140
00:07:46,520 --> 00:07:48,540
I just can't do the sea, no matter what.

141
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:49,880
Because...

142
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:51,040
Because...

143
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:53,620
Because if I wear a bikini,

144
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:56,380
everyone will see that
my chest is totally flat.

145
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:03,760
But if I'm with Ryo-sama, whether it's
mountains or rivers, it'll surely be a fun trip.

146
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:06,200
What I want is the sea.

147
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:09,880
And there's one more, an even stronger ally.

148
00:08:09,880 --> 00:08:14,600
You're finished. You're dead meat.

149
00:08:15,220 --> 00:08:18,220
You're a man, yet you'd betray us?

150
00:08:18,220 --> 00:08:20,980
Ryotsu, the sea is certainly wonderful.

151
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:23,860
Honestly, I want to go too.

152
00:08:23,860 --> 00:08:25,000
Then why?

153
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:29,720
Think about it: at the beach there's a
group of college girls with great bodies.

154
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,740
Isn't that wonderful?

155
00:08:31,740 --> 00:08:32,620
Naive.

156
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:36,680
Imagine that appearing right in front of me.

157
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:39,760
Well, not yet, I mean -

158
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:44,760
You'll drown in a sea of nosebleeds
before you even get in the ocean!

159
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:46,180
I-I see.

160
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:47,940
Pathetic.

161
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:52,960
So, just this once,
I'll be taking the women's side.

162
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:56,480
That's a troublesome
bunch we've got against us.

163
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:59,520
But we should still have the advantage.

164
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:05,260
With these two on our side, we might
win even if I don't have to go all out.

165
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:09,100
Now then, I'll explain the rules.

166
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:11,660
Basically, it's hide-and-seek.

167
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:14,540
First, we'll play rock-paper-scissors
to decide who's the tagger.

168
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:18,280
The match starts once someone
other than the tagger kicks this can.

169
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:23,520
The tagger retrieves the can

170
00:09:24,260 --> 00:09:27,700
and sets it back in its original
spot while the others hide.

171
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:32,400
When the tagger finds someone,
they hurry back to the can and stomp on it.

172
00:09:32,940 --> 00:09:35,260
At that moment, you must always shout
"Pokopen!"

173
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:38,220
Like this: "Nakagawa found! Pokopen!"

174
00:09:38,220 --> 00:09:40,760
What does that mean?

175
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:42,520
Well, that is...

176
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:43,560
You don't know?

177
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:44,300
It's just "pen."

178
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:46,520
The meaning doesn't matter at all!

179
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:54,460
Where I'm from, it was pokopen too.
Mine was just calling out names, though.

180
00:09:54,940 --> 00:10:00,080
In my village, we stomped three times and chanted,
"Who's that? Who's that? One, two, three!"

181
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:10,020
The game ends once everyone's been found. But if someone who hasn't been found kicks the can,
everything's wiped out.

182
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:13,540
Then let's actually try it once.

183
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:15,880
Janken-pon! Aiko desho!

184
00:10:18,260 --> 00:10:19,780
Looks like a tie

185
00:10:19,780 --> 00:10:20,820
Alright, here we go.

186
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:22,660
Wait, you're the one kicking?

187
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:24,960
Oh my!

188
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:27,240
Go!

189
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,940
Geez, that idiot's brute strength.

190
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:39,260
Just an ordinary park.

191
00:10:41,020 --> 00:10:45,000
Right, I can pretty much figure
out where amateurs would hide.

192
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:52,260
Found you!

193
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:53,460
On!

194
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:56,200
1, 2, 3.

195
00:10:56,620 --> 00:11:00,020
Hold on, didn't you just say "Pokopen"?

196
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:01,740
I did say it.

197
00:11:01,740 --> 00:11:03,380
No, I didn't say it.

198
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:06,780
No, I'm pretty sure you said "1, 2, 3."

199
00:11:06,780 --> 00:11:09,220
Oops, out of childhood habit I just...

200
00:11:10,260 --> 00:11:12,600
And it seems you also
stomped the can three times.

201
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:16,200
I'm not used to it,
so I had to re-stomp it over and over.

202
00:11:16,766 --> 00:11:21,300
Now that I think about it, I've heard
there's a place that has a three-stomp rule.

203
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:22,780
Komachi, you really are...

204
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:25,300
I told you, I've never played it before.

205
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:28,500
Well, whatever, today's just practice.

206
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:31,340
If you make a mistake in the real match,
I'll be checking strictly.

207
00:11:31,340 --> 00:11:34,500
Fine, then let's start again.

208
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:36,740
Both toes, go! Pokopen!

209
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:40,340
Whoa, th-that's dirty!
Since when is that allowed?

210
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:43,420
It's your fault for not hiding faster.

211
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:44,816
Damn it, this humiliation...

212
00:11:44,866 --> 00:11:47,760
I'll pay you back many times over in the real match,
you hear?

213
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:51,500
Hmph, I'll definitely find
you in the real match too!

214
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:09,335
Now then, will the Katsushika
station's staff trip be at the beach,

215
00:12:09,385 --> 00:12:10,600
or in the mountains?

216
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:13,260
The time of the decisive
battle has finally arrived.

217
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:17,200
Here at Kameari Park,
crowds of spectators have gathered,

218
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:20,460
eagerly awaiting the start of the match.

219
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:26,460
Joining us in the broadcast booth are Station
Chief Honda Gomes and Chief Ohara Daijirō.

220
00:12:26,460 --> 00:12:26,960
Hello.

221
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:30,920
Are you two hoping for the beach,
or the mountains?

222
00:12:30,920 --> 00:12:36,380
Well, I'm happy to go wherever
the station's staff would like.

223
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:38,200
Me too.

224
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:43,520
These two had hidden their true
feelings behind their public stances.

225
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:48,980
And here comes the referee,
Chief Ishizu Tetsuo!

226
00:12:48,980 --> 00:12:50,640
Player introductions.

227
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:55,000
First, carrying the hopes of
the men's team on his shoulders,

228
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,500
here comes the Uni team!

229
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:58,100
The captain is Kankichi Ryotsu.

230
00:12:58,100 --> 00:13:00,140
Behind him is Nakagawa Keiichi.

231
00:13:00,140 --> 00:13:01,100
Honda Shun.

232
00:13:01,100 --> 00:13:02,260
Terai Yōichi.

233
00:13:02,260 --> 00:13:05,000
followed by the four players,
including Sanedera Tatsunosuke.

234
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:06,120
Good luck!

235
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:07,520
It's the beach, no question!

236
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:11,060
The mountain team!
Their captain is Ono no Komachi.

237
00:13:11,060 --> 00:13:15,160
Next are Sei Shōnagon,
Reiko Akimoto, and Asato Ai.

238
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:17,580
And here is Orubō Saigō of Kokuichi-ten.

239
00:13:24,260 --> 00:13:26,320
It feels like the scent
of the sea is drifting in.

240
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:28,320
This is the delicious highland air,
isn't it?

241
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:32,080
Now, let me explain the rules.

242
00:13:32,540 --> 00:13:35,140
First, the sea team,
going first, sends out one tagger.

243
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:37,020
Everyone on the mountain team hides.

244
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:41,680
If the tagger finds everyone within 10 minutes,
the tagger wins.

245
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:44,240
Otherwise, it's a loss for the tagger.

246
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:47,220
We'll do this five times each,
changing the location.

247
00:13:47,220 --> 00:13:51,260
At the end, the team with more
wins is declared the victor.

248
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:54,920
And don't forget to shout
"Pokopen" when you stomp the can.

249
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:58,000
Now, the sea team's tagger, step forward.

250
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,620
Just what we've been waiting for,
Mr. President!

251
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:04,540
They threw their ace at us right away

252
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:07,680
Don't worry,
I'm not losing to someone like that.

253
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:14,120
And now, the sea team goes first, with captain
Kankichi Ryotsu making his grand entrance!

254
00:14:15,060 --> 00:14:19,180
Ryotsu, who said before the match
that he was 200% confident of winning,

255
00:14:19,660 --> 00:14:23,140
will he show us the skill
to back up those words?

256
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:24,060
Here I go.

257
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:25,220
Good luck, I'm counting on you.

258
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:26,640
The match begins!

259
00:14:31,140 --> 00:14:32,220
Whiffed it.

260
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:37,140
Whoa, Volvo, did you get nervous at the end?

261
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:39,560
Hurry up and hide!

262
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:40,740
That's the last one.

263
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:43,580
Found Naoko! Pongoben!

264
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:45,220
Found Volvo! Pongoben!

265
00:14:46,980 --> 00:14:48,820
You two, into the cell!

266
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:54,120
They can't have hidden far yet.

267
00:14:56,180 --> 00:14:57,800
Found Reiko! Pongoben!

268
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:02,280
Found Maria! Pongoben!

269
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:03,280
This is amazing.

270
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:05,060
Found all four in no time.

271
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:08,620
Honestly,
I wish you'd work this hard on a normal day.

272
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:14,980
Typical of someone
raised in the old downtown

273
00:15:15,540 --> 00:15:18,020
But from where I'm standing,
you've still got a long way to go.

274
00:15:18,020 --> 00:15:19,660
Your bag's a mess.

275
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:22,240
Gotcha.

276
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,360
Damn it.

277
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:26,980
I knew you'd jump out the moment
I left an opening behind me.

278
00:15:28,340 --> 00:15:30,960
To think my movements were read like that.

279
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:32,000
Haa.

280
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:35,660
Komachi, found! Pokopen!

281
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:39,880
That's it, the tagger wins.

282
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:41,820
He did it, Ryo-chan!

283
00:15:41,820 --> 00:15:44,340
In less than two minutes, he found everyone.

284
00:15:44,900 --> 00:15:46,000
A total victory.

285
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:50,260
That I, of all people, would lose like this!

286
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:52,600
It's not Komachi's fault.

287
00:15:53,260 --> 00:15:56,360
That's right,
this game is unfair to civilized people.

288
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:58,580
If only I hadn't kicked the can.

289
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,840
Besides, the match isn't over yet.

290
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:04,480
Mountain team, the oni, step forward!

291
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:07,000
Then, as planned, I'll go.

292
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:08,100
Good luck.

293
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:09,060
What?

294
00:16:09,720 --> 00:16:11,220
Is that really okay?

295
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:13,440
Just watch out for Ryotsu's moves.

296
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:15,980
I know, leave it to me.

297
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:20,840
No good, Naoko can't win.
The experience gap is too big.

298
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:21,420
Go!

299
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:24,560
Start!

300
00:16:25,460 --> 00:16:27,340
Nakagawa, how mean!

301
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:28,140
Okay, hide!

302
00:16:31,020 --> 00:16:33,100
Let's see, is it this way?

303
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:37,340
That was so careless, Naoko.

304
00:16:37,340 --> 00:16:39,920
From that spot,
they'll get your back easily.

305
00:16:41,820 --> 00:16:42,720
Uh-oh, uh-oh.

306
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:43,840
Naoko.

307
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:45,360
Kankichi Ryotsu.

308
00:16:47,060 --> 00:16:48,600
Amateurs, step aside.

309
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,420
Player Ryotsu.

310
00:16:52,420 --> 00:16:55,480
The match was decided before
the tagger found a single hider.

311
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:58,220
Is it going to be a one-sided affair?

312
00:16:58,580 --> 00:17:02,280
Ryotsu shows an unusual talent when it comes to these things,
you know.

313
00:17:02,860 --> 00:17:05,300
So the staff trip will be at the sea, then.

314
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:08,920
Now, let's begin round two.

315
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:13,120
Honda, you're the tagger next!
Show them the power of the shitamachi!

316
00:17:13,120 --> 00:17:14,320
Yes, senpai!

317
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:16,000
Alright, this time for sure.

318
00:17:16,420 --> 00:17:17,660
Good luck, Volvo-san!

319
00:17:18,860 --> 00:17:19,500
Wait a second.

320
00:17:20,620 --> 00:17:23,400
Shouldn't Maria-chan be
the one to kick the can here?

321
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:24,520
I'll do it.

322
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:27,120
Right, she's a former kickboxer, after all.

323
00:17:27,460 --> 00:17:27,780
I see.

324
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:31,500
Also, Maria-chan,
can you show me your shoes for a moment?

325
00:17:32,740 --> 00:17:33,360
Go!

326
00:17:34,540 --> 00:17:35,400
Here I come!

327
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:42,320
What a powerful kick!
That's an incredible distance!

328
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:46,320
As expected from a former kickboxer.

329
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:50,040
Still, it's flying too far!
Could he possibly have...

330
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:54,500
He really did stick a metal piece on it!

331
00:17:55,140 --> 00:17:57,020
Does attaching metal make it fly farther?

332
00:17:58,580 --> 00:17:59,460
It's the same as striking it.

333
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:00,160
I see.

334
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:03,560
When I was a kid, that was banned.

335
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:06,100
I never expected them to
resort to a trick like this.

336
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:10,820
I found them.

337
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:12,000
Too slow.

338
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:14,680
That's it.

339
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:16,660
Time's up, the tagger loses.

340
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:17,740
Yay!

341
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:20,280
If you're using a metal piece,
then this is what I'll do.

342
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:22,600
I touched it.

343
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:25,880
Come on, give me a break.

344
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:27,660
What kind of person does that?

345
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:31,260
With heavy geta,
the distance shoots up explosively.

346
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:34,080
This technique only works with
a caveman's brute strength.

347
00:18:34,980 --> 00:18:37,260
Akimoto is finally back.

348
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:42,680
But the time limit has long since passed.

349
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:46,600
And here the captains of both teams
have been called over by the referee.

350
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:52,220
From now on, kicking the can with metal,
wood, stone, or similar objects is prohibited.

351
00:18:52,220 --> 00:18:54,580
As expected, it's a ban.

352
00:18:54,580 --> 00:18:57,960
What? If we just play normally,
we should be able to win easily.

353
00:18:58,580 --> 00:19:00,100
The next tagger is Terai, right?

354
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:00,800
Yeah.

355
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:02,940
Show them the strength
of experienced players.

356
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:05,340
Now the other side has the advantage

357
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:07,740
What? Komachi.

358
00:19:07,740 --> 00:19:11,300
I just thought of something. How about this?

359
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:13,480
Hide quickly!

360
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:15,360
Come on, Terai, go pick it up quickly!

361
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:17,000
Yes!

362
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,700
Now, Terai has begun the search.

363
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:26,100
I hope he conducts a steady,
methodical search.

364
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:31,600
Doko-san!

365
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:33,320
Pikke-pokopen!

366
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:35,700
Too bad, it's me!

367
00:19:35,700 --> 00:19:37,680
Maria-san!

368
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:40,680
Mistaken identity, so the tagger loses.

369
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:41,980
You idiot!

370
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:45,820
Changing your hairstyle or clothes to fool the tagger is the most basic of basics,
you know!

371
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:47,500
Sorry, I slipped up.

372
00:19:47,500 --> 00:19:48,240
Damn it!

373
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:51,380
I did it, just like Komachi-chan said!

374
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:52,660
Our plan worked.

375
00:19:52,660 --> 00:19:53,700
Wow!

376
00:19:53,700 --> 00:19:55,880
It's just a matter of
using your head a little.

377
00:19:55,880 --> 00:19:56,520
Hey, Komatsu.

378
00:19:56,520 --> 00:19:59,540
You're not an experienced player after all,
are you?

379
00:20:00,180 --> 00:20:01,600
I've told you, I'm not.

380
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:03,340
Such a rustic, countrified game.

381
00:20:03,340 --> 00:20:05,300
How would I know it, obviously?

382
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:06,560
I see.

383
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:15,460
The offense and defense
continue in perfect unison.

384
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:18,540
Neither tagger is able to win easily.

385
00:20:33,180 --> 00:20:35,620
The sea team's final attack also failed.

386
00:20:35,620 --> 00:20:38,080
Now, the mountain team's last attack.

387
00:20:38,080 --> 00:20:40,980
If the oni loses here, the sea team wins.

388
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:44,080
If they win,
it goes into sudden-death overtime.

389
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:48,480
The final oni is mountain
team captain Komachi Ono.

390
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:51,320
However,
she has no kan-keri experience at all.

391
00:20:51,320 --> 00:20:52,700
The mountain team is in trouble.

392
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:55,120
Looks like the sea team's winning.

393
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:58,360
It's Honda's game now.

394
00:20:59,220 --> 00:21:00,860
Well, if it's come to this,
there's no choice.

395
00:21:00,860 --> 00:21:03,580
Komachi absolutely cannot afford to lose.

396
00:21:08,860 --> 00:21:10,040
Found you, Nakagawa!

397
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:11,880
Found you, Terai!

398
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:13,260
Pokopen!

399
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:14,660
Found you, Honda!

400
00:21:14,660 --> 00:21:18,040
She's finding them at an incredible,
relentless pace!

401
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:19,700
Found you, Sanedera!

402
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:20,200
What?

403
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:22,540
Pokopen!

404
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:26,000
Komachi has already found four of them!

405
00:21:27,520 --> 00:21:27,820
That's all.

406
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:32,380
Four of them in an instant!

407
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:35,320
Komachi,
she really isn't someone to underestimate.

408
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:37,760
But I'll be the one who laughs last.

409
00:21:37,760 --> 00:21:40,260
I'll show you the ultimate secret
technique of the old downtown.

410
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:42,400
Where are you, Kankichi Ryotsu?

411
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:49,820
Ryotsu...

412
00:21:49,820 --> 00:21:50,440
Whoa!

413
00:21:52,500 --> 00:21:53,420
A decoy?

414
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:55,060
The sound of sandals...

415
00:21:55,060 --> 00:21:56,160
There he is!

416
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:57,920
A cat?

417
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:00,420
A monkey? Come on, not a monkey!

418
00:22:00,420 --> 00:22:03,080
Where on earth are you, Ryotsu?

419
00:22:04,080 --> 00:22:04,980
Stop!

420
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:07,040
Damn it!

421
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:08,340
The helm is mine!

422
00:22:08,860 --> 00:22:10,280
This is an unexpected tactic.

423
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:11,460
Senior, moving!

424
00:22:11,460 --> 00:22:13,520
Komachi, hurry!

425
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:15,280
No good, we won't make it.

426
00:22:15,280 --> 00:22:17,200
Past the ship, I can see the sea!

427
00:22:25,520 --> 00:22:31,120
Whoa! No way!
It's covering the top of the stake!

428
00:22:31,540 --> 00:22:32,780
Get out!

429
00:22:33,740 --> 00:22:36,440
Me, the one they call the Kan-keri Komachi!

430
00:22:37,080 --> 00:22:39,440
Did you say Kan-keri Komachi?

431
00:22:39,580 --> 00:22:40,400
You, Komachi!

432
00:22:40,880 --> 00:22:44,380
I've got my pride too,
as the man they call Ryotsu the Kan-keri!

433
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:47,060
You're still going to kick with that leg?

434
00:22:47,360 --> 00:22:49,320
I won't lose! Absolutely not!

435
00:22:49,680 --> 00:22:50,580
Ryotsu!

436
00:22:50,900 --> 00:22:51,380
Komachi!

437
00:22:51,380 --> 00:22:52,380
Cheek!

438
00:22:53,760 --> 00:22:54,820
Chocopie!

439
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:56,460
Can you get it out?

440
00:22:57,140 --> 00:22:57,580
Yes.

441
00:22:59,700 --> 00:23:00,520
Gyaaah!

442
00:23:04,400 --> 00:23:06,560
That's it, the taggers lose.

443
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:10,040
The kan-keri match ends 1-0,
the sea team wins!

444
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:11,140
Yay!

445
00:23:15,760 --> 00:23:17,260
Kan-keri Komachi!

446
00:23:17,260 --> 00:23:19,780
It's like I've lost at
kan-keri for the first time.

447
00:23:21,380 --> 00:23:23,460
Wow, we won!

448
00:23:43,720 --> 00:23:46,760
Well, the sea team's pretty fun, isn't it?

449
00:23:46,760 --> 00:23:49,060
Yeah, well,

450
00:23:51,060 --> 00:23:52,720
there's just nobody else!

451
00:23:55,140 --> 00:23:55,940
Here it comes!

452
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:58,420
We won because of me, obviously!

453
00:23:58,420 --> 00:24:00,400
Move the trip schedule!

454
00:24:21,180 --> 00:24:27,340
With you, I wake up feeling good.

455
00:24:28,040 --> 00:24:31,760
Even boring stories

456
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:36,560
set my whole body on fire.

457
00:24:36,780 --> 00:24:43,200
But I want to see my friends.

458
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:47,160
I surely want to be loved.

459
00:24:47,160 --> 00:24:52,580
to the point that everyone
gets a little annoyed,

460
00:24:53,160 --> 00:24:58,320
feeling like we're melting into each other.

461
00:24:58,320 --> 00:25:02,300
I surely want to confess.

462
00:25:02,300 --> 00:25:07,960
For some reason, only in love am I timid.

463
00:25:07,960 --> 00:25:11,480
Pretending to be tough

464
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:15,820
Don't hide everything.

465
00:25:42,260 --> 00:25:43,660
Thank you for watching.

